            %p
              where in the last step we used the constraints on degrees given by def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LabelConfigurationSpace"}
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle-,-\rangle
              satisfies the defining equation of an invariant polynomial on the proper configuration space. The non-degeneracy is due to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:NonDegeneracyOfInnerProduct"} (2)
          %p
            From the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            in the section
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element#CanonicalChernSimonsElement"} Canonical Chern-Simons element
            we have that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory"} infinity-Chern-Simons theory
            defined by the data
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, \langle -,-\rangle)
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo +
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L : A \mapsto
                  \\langle A,  d A\rangle
                  +
                  \\sum_{k = 1}^\infty
                  \\frac{2}{(k+1)!}
                  \\langle A , [A, \cdots , A]_k\rangle
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebroid+valued+differential+form"} valued differential form
            on some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %h2#OpenClosedStringFieldTheory Open-Closed string field theory
          %p
            When considering open and closed strings jointly, then in addition to the closed string sector being encoded by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi closed
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_{closed}
            as above, the open string sector is encoded in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} A-∞ algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi open
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{open}
            and the former acts on the latter by homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "derivation#OfAlgebrasOverADGOperad"} derivations on algebras over a dg-operad
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi closed
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi open
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathfrak{g}_{closed} \longrightarrow Der (A_{open})
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#KajiuraStasheff04"}> Kajiura-Stasheff 04
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Markl04"} Markl 04
          %p
            Notice that this is half of the axioms of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Rinehart+pair"} Lie-Rinehart pair
          %h2#SuperstringFieldTheory Superstring field theory
          %p
            The maybe most wide-spread attempt to generalize the above to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            field theory replaces the Chern-Simons-type action with a
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-type+superstring+field+theory"} WZW-type superstring field theory
            \.
          %p
            A formulation of superstring field theory more on line with the Chern-Simons type bosonic theory is proposed in (
            %a{:href => "#JurcoMuenster13"}> Jurco-Muenster 13
            ). See also the introduction there for a survey of the literature
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 1d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 3d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 4d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 6d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7d Chern-Simons theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-models"} AKSZ sigma-models
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} infinite-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Closed string field theory has been argued to arise from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loops"} Wilson loops
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/IKKT+matrix+model"} IKKT matrix model
            in (
            %a{:href => "#FukumaKawaiKitazawaTsuchiya97"}> Fukuma-Kawai-Kitazawa-Tsuchiya 97
            )
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Introduction and survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Rastelli"}> Leonardo Rastelli
                ,
                %em String Field Theory
                in
                %em Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0509129"}> arXiv:hep-th/0509129
                )
            %li
              %p
                W. Siegel,
                %em Introduction to string field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0107094"}> arXiv:hep-th/0107094
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                %em String Field Theory as World-sheet UV Regulator
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.00263"}> arXiv:1902.00263
                )
            %li#Erbin20a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harold+Erbin"}> Harold Erbin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Field Theory – A Modern Introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 980
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.01686"} arXiv:2301.01686
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-65321-7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-65321-7
            %li#Erbin20b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harold+Erbin"}> Harold Erbin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String theory: a field theory perspective
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lpthe.jussieu.fr/~erbin/files/reviews/string_theory.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harold+Erbin"}> Harold Erbin
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://string-field-theory.org/"} String Field Theory – Website
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Four Lectures on Closed String Field Theory
                %strong 851
                (2020) 1-36 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.06785"}> arXiv:1905.06785
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2020.01.003"} doi:10.1016/j.physrep.2020.01.003
            %li
              %p
                Carlo Maccaferri,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Field Theory
                %em Oxford Research Encyclopedia of Physics
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.00875"}> arXiv:2308.00875
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Field Theory: A Review
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Quantum+Gravity"} Handbook of Quantum Gravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.19421"} arXiv:2405.19421
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-19-3079-9"} doi:10.1007/978-981-19-3079-9
          %h3#ReferencesBosonicSFT Bosonic string field theory
          %h4#ReferencesBosonocOSFT Open SFT
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Witten86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative Geometry and String Field Theory
                %strong 268
                (1986) 253-294 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(86)90155-0"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(86)90155-0
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote.un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
                %p
                  (cf. also
                  %a{:href => "fusion+bundle#RelationToStringFieldTheory"} here
                  at
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+bundle"} fusion bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On background independent open string field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9208027"} arXiv:hep-th/9208027
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Matej Kudrna,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"} Martin Schnabl
              %em Universal Solutions in Open String Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.03221"}> arXiv:1812.03221
              )
          %p
            On a proposal for a background-independent formalism for bosonic open string field theory, exhibiting in particular the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthosymplectic+super+Lie+algebra"} orthosymplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi OSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} OSp(d|2)
            as a symmetry:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Itzhak+Bars"}> Itzhak Bars
              , Dmitry Rychkov.
              %em Background Independent String Field Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1407.4699"}> arXiv:1407.4699
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#ReferencesBosonicCSFT Closed SFT
          %p The fundamental work of Zwiebach on closed SFT is summed up in
          %ul
            %li#Zwiebach93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"}> Barton Zwiebach
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Closed string field theory: Quantum action and the Batalin-Vilkovisky master equation
              %strong 390
              1 (1993) 33-152 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9206084"}> arXiv:hep-th/9206084
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(93)90388-6"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(93)90388-6
          %p Brief reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"}> Barton Zwiebach
              ,
              %em Closed String Field Theory: An Introduction
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9305026"}> arXiv:hep-th/9305026
              )
          %p
            The explicit identification of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            coupled to the action for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton"} dilaton
            in the lowest orders of the CSFT action is discussed for instance in
            %a{:href => "#YangZwiebach"} Yang-Zwiebach, section 3.1
            and in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Bang-Gui Liu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em General coordinate transformation and gravitational action from closed bosonic string field theory
            %li
              %p
                Masako Asano, Mitsuhiro Kato,
                %em Closed string field theory in a-gauge
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.3901"}> arXiv:1206.3901
                )
          %p
            Discussion of the expected closed string tachyon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            is in
          %ul
            %li#YangZwiebach
              %p
                Haitang Yang,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Closed String Tachyon Vacuum ?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0506077"} arXiv:hep-th/0506077
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Moeller"}> Nicolas Moeller
                , Haitang Yang,
                %em The nonperturbative closed string tachyon vacuum to high level
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0609208"}> arXiv:hep-th/0609208
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Moeller"}> Nicolas Moeller
                ,
                %em A tachyon lump in closed string field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.0697"}> arXiv:0804.0697
                )
          %p and further detailed analysis is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Moeller"}> Nicolas Moeller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Closed Bosonic String Field Theory at Quintic Order: Five-Tachyon Contact Term and Dilaton Theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0609209"} arXiv:hep-th/0609209
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Moeller"}> Nicolas Moeller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Closed Bosonic String Field Theory at Quintic Order II: Marginal Deformations and Effective Potential
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.2102"} arXiv:0705.2102
          %h3#ReferencesSuperstringFieldTheory Superstring field theory
          %p
            The generalization to field theory for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/picture+number"} picture number
            compliates the
            = succeed "-sector," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
          %ul
            %li
              Hiroshi Kunitomo, Yuji Okawa,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Complete action for open superstring field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.00366"} arXiv:1508.00366
          %p A survey is in
          %ul
            %li#Okawa16
              Yuji Okawa,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Recent developments in the construction of superstring field theory I
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www-het.ph.tsukuba.ac.jp/~ishibash/SFT16/okawa.pdf"} pdf
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li#ErlerKonopkaSach13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                , Sebastian Konopka,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"} Ivo Sachs
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Resolving Witten’s Superstring Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.2948"} arXiv:1312.2948
            %li#ErlerKonopkaSach14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                , Sebastian Konopka,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"} Ivo Sachs
                = succeed "," do
                  %em NS-NS Sector of Closed Superstring Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1403.0940"} arXiv:1403.0940
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                %em Gauge Invariant 1PI Effective Superstring Field Theory: Inclusion of the Ramond Sector
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.00988"}> arXiv:1501.00988
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                , Sebastian Konopka,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"} Ivo Sachs
                %em Ramond Equations of Motion in Superstring Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.05774"}> arXiv:1506.05774
                )
            %li#Sen15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BV Master Action for Heterotic and Type II String Field Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1508.05387"} arXiv:1508.05387
          %p with further developments in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Yuji Okawa,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                %em Heterotic String Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406212"}> arXiv:hep-th/0406212
                )
            %li
              %p
                Roji Pius,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"} Ashoke Sen
                %em Cutkosky Rules for Superstring Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1604.01783"}> arXiv:1604.01783
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                %em Reality of Superstring Field Theory Action
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03455"}> arXiv:1606.03455
                )
            %li
              %p
                Hiroshi Kunitomo, Tatsuya Sugimoto,
                %em Type II superstring field theory with cyclic L-infinity structure
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.04103"}> arxiv:1911.04103
                )
          %p
            Interpretation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/picture+number"} picture number
            as a grading on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+on+supermanifolds"} differential forms on supermanifolds
            induced from a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+over+supermanifolds"} integral top form
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Belopolsky"}> Alexander Belopolsky
              ,
              %em Picture changing operators in supergeometry and superstring theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706033"}> arXiv:hep-th/9706033
              ).
          %p and has been further amplified in
          %ul
            %li#Witten12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , appendix D of
                %em Notes On Super Riemann Surfaces And Their Moduli
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.2459"}> arXiv:1209.2459
                )
            %li
              %p
                R. Catenacci, P.A. Grassi, S. Noja,
                %em Superstring Field Theory, Superforms and Supergeometry
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.09563"}> arXiv:1807.09563
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Background Independence of Closed Superstring Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.08468"} arXiv:1711.08468
            %li
              %p
                Corinne de Lacroix, Harold Erbin, Sitender Pratap Kashyap,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"} Ashoke Sen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Closed Superstring Field Theory and its Applications
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.06410"} arXiv:1703.06410
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ranveer+Kumar+Singh"}> Ranveer Kumar Singh
                \:
                %em Algebraic Structures In Closed Superstring Field Theory, Homotopy Transfer And Effective Actions
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.08063"}> arXiv:2405.08063
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p For previous constructions, the introduction of
          %ul
            %li#JurcoMuenster13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"}> Branislav Jurco
              , Korbinian Muenster,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Type II Superstring Field Theory: Geometric Approach and Operadic Description
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.2323"} arXiv/1303.2323
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/JHEP04(2013)126"} doi
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li#Yeh93
              Chungsheng James Yeh,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topics in superstring theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/366138"} SPIRE
          %p has a useful survey, which we quote now:
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %h6#quote_from_jurcomuenster13
              Quote from (
              %a{:href => "#JurcoMuenster13"}> Jurco-Muenster13
              ):
            %p The first attempt towards a field theory of superstrings was initiated by the work of Witten
            %ul
              %li#Witten86a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interacting field theory of open superstrings
            %p
              by seeking a Chern-Simons like action for open superstrings similar to the one of open bosonic string field theory (
              %a{:href => "#Witten86"}> Witten 86
              ). The major obstacle compared to the bosonic string is the necessity of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/picture+changing+operators"} picture changing operators
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Witten86a"} Witten 86a
            %ul
              %li
                C. Wendt,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Scattering amplitudes and contact interactions in Witten’s superstring field theory
            %p In order to circumvent this problem, another approach was pursued which sets the string field into a different picture
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  C.R. Preitschopf, C.B. Thorn, S. Yost,
                  %em Superstring field theory
                  Nuclear Physics B, Volume 337, Issue 2.
              %li
                %p
                  I.Ya. Aref’eva, P.B. Medvedev, A.P. Zubarev,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em New representation for string field solves the consistency problem for open superstring field theory
            %p
              but upon including the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} Ramond sector
            %ul
              %li
                M. Kroyter,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstring field theory equivalence: Ramond sector
            %p
              These two approaches are based on the small Hilbert space, the state space including the reparametrization
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghosts"} ghosts
              and superghosts as they arise from gaugefixing. Upon
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonization"} bosonization
              of the superghosts, an additional zero mode arises which allows the formulation of a WZW like action for the NS sector of open superstring field theory
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Super-Poincare Invariant Superstring Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503099"} hep-th/9503099
            %p
              In contrast to bosonic string field theory,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV+quantization"} BV quantization
              of this theory is more intricate than simply relaxing the ghost number constraint for the fields of the classical action
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Constrained BV description of string field theory
              %li
                %p
                  M. Kroyter, Y. Okawa, M. Schnabl, S. Torii,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                  %em Open superstring eld theory I: gauge xing, ghost structure, and propagator, Journal of High Energy Physics, Volume 2012, Issue 3.
            %p Finally, there is a formulation of open superstring field theory that differs from all other approaches in not fixing the picture of classical fields
            %ul
              %li
                M. Kroyter,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstring field theory in the democratic picture
            %p
              On the other hand, the construction of bosonic closed string field theory (
              %a{:href => "#Zwiebach"}> Zwiebach 92
              ) takes its origin in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              of closed
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi b
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_0^- = 0
              constraint.
            %p
              In an almost unnoticed work (
              %a{:href => "#Yeh93"}> Yeh
              ), the geometric approach developed in bosonic closed string field theory, as described in the previous paragraph, has been generalized to the context of superstring field theory. Neveu-Schwarz punctures behave quite similar to punctures in the bosonic case, but a Ramond puncture describes a divisor on a super Riemann surface rather than a point. As a consequence, local coordinates around Ramond punctures, globally defined over super moduli space, can be fixed only up to rotations and translation in the Ramond divisor.
            %p A given background provides forms on super moduli space
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Belopolsky"}> Alexander Belopolsky
                  ,
                  %em New Geometrical Approach to Superstrings
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9703183"}> arXiv:hep-th/9703183
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  L. Alvarez-Gaume, P. Nelson, C. Gomez, G. Sierra, C. Vafa,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Fermionic strings in the operator formalism
            %p
              in the sense of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+over+supermanifolds"} geometric integration theory on supermanifolds
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/picture+changing+operators"} picture changing operators
              has been clarified
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Belopolsky"}> Alexander Belopolsky
                ,
                %em Picture changing operators in supergeometry and superstring theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706033"}> arXiv:hep-th/9706033
                ).
            %p
              Integrating along an odd direction in moduli space inevitably generates a picture changing operator. Thus, the ambiguity of defining local coordinates around Ramond punctures produces a picture changing operator associated with the vector field generating translations in the Ramond divisor. The bpz inner product plus the additional insertions originating from the sewing define the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
              relevant for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV+quantization"} BV quantization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi b
                      %mn 0
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_0^- = 0
              constraint on the state space. The purpose of (
              %a{:href => "#JurcoMuenster13"}> Jurco-Muenster 13
              ) is to describe the construction of type II superstring field theory in the geometric approach.
          %p Older reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
              ,
              %em Review of open superstring field theory
              , (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0105230"}> arXiv:hep-th/0105230
              )
          %p More recently there is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Tomoyuki Takezaki,
                %em Open superstring field theory including the Ramond sector based on the supermoduli space
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.02176"}> arXiv:1901.02176
                )
            %li
              %p
                Hiroshi Kunitomo,
                %em Type II superstring field theory revisited
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.07917"}> arXiv:2106.07917
                )
          %h3#effective_field_theory Effective field theory
          %p
            Discussion of Wilsonian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            of string field theory includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                R. Brustein, S.P.De Alwis,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalization group equation and non-perturbative effects in string-field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(91)90451-3"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(91)90451-3
            %li
              %p
                Brustein and K. Roland,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Space-time versus world sheet renormalization group equation in string theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(92)90317-5"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(92)90317-5
            %li#Sen16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wilsonian Effective Action of Superstring Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.00459"} arXiv:1609.00459
          %h3#ReferencesHomotopyAlgebra
            Relation to
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} L-infinity algebra
            structure on Zwiebach’s bosonic closed string fields is apparently due to a comment by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
            to the conference contribution
          %ul
            %li#Zwiebach89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"}> Barton Zwiebach
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Issues In Covariant Closed String Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Proceedings of
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/966930"} 10th and Final Workshop on Grand Unification
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/282685"} spire:282685
          %p It appears in print in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"}> Barton Zwiebach
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Closed string field theory: Quantum action and the Batalin-Vilkovisky master equation
              %strong 390
              1 (1993) 33-152 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9206084"}> arXiv:hep-th/9206084
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(93)90388-6"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(93)90388-6
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras+in+physics"} L-infinity algebras in physics
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"} A-infinity algebra
            structure of bosonic open string field theory in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Gaberdiel"}> Matthias Gaberdiel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
              %em Tensor Constructions of Open String Theories I: Foundations
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705038"}> arXiv:hep-th/9705038
              )
          %p For the topological string see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manfred+Herbst"}> Manfred Herbst
              ,
              %em Quantum A-infinity Structures for Open-Closed Topological Strings
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0602018"}> arXiv:hep-th/0602018
              )
          %p
            Discussion for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic
            string field theory is in
          %ul
            %li#KunitomoSugimoto19
              Hiroshi Kunitomo, Tatsuya Sugimoto,
              %em Heterotic string field theory with cyclic L-infinity structure
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.02991"}> arXiv:1902.02991
              )
          %p Discussion of the mathematical aspects is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                ,
                %em Closed string field theory, strong homotopy Lie algebras and the operad actions of moduli space
                Talk given at the
                %em Conference on Topics in Geometry and Physics
                (1992) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9304061"}> arXiv:hep-th/9304061
                )
            %li#Markl
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"}> Martin Markl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Loop Homotopy Algebras in Closed String Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711045"} arXiv:hep-th/9711045
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Tomasiello"}> Alessandro Tomasiello
                ,
                %em A-infinity structure and superpotentials
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0107195"}> arXiv:hep-th/0107195
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshige+Kajiura"}> Hiroshige Kajiura
                ,
                %em Homotopy Algebra Morphism and Geometry of Classical String Field Theory
                (2001) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0112228"}> arXiv:hep-th/0112228
                )
            %li#KajiuraStasheff04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshige+Kajiura"}> Hiroshige Kajiura
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy algebras inspired by classical open-closed string field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0410291"} arXiv:math/0410291
            %li#Markl04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"}> Martin Markl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Operadic interpretation of
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#KajiuraStasheff04"} Kajiura-Stasheff 04
            %li
              %p
                Korbinian Münster,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"} Ivo Sachs
                %em Quantum Open-Closed Homotopy Algebra and String Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.4101"}> arXiv:1109.4101
                )
            %li
              %p
                Korbinian Münster,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"} Ivo Sachs
                %em On Homotopy Algebras and Quantum String Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.3444"}> arXiv:1303.3444
                )
            %li#DoubekJurcoMuenster13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Doubek"}> Martin Doubek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"} Branislav Jurco
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modular operads and the quantum open-closed homotopy algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.3223"} arXiv:1308.3223
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP12(2015)158"} doi:10.1007/JHEP12(2015)158
          %p Surveys include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Cohomological+Physics"} A Survey of Cohomological Physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshige+Kajiura"}> Hiroshige Kajiura
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                %em Homotopy algebra of open–closed strings
                Geometry &amp; Topology Monographs 13 (2008) 229–259 (
                %a{:href => "http://msp.warwick.ac.uk/gtm/2008/13/gtm-2008-13-010s.pdf"}> pdf
                ) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0606283"}> arXiv:hep-th/0606283
                )
            %li#Sachs15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"}> Ivo Sachs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String theory and homotopy algebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.muni.cz/~srni/Prednasky/Sachs.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Sachs19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivo+Sachs"}> Ivo Sachs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy Algebras in String Field Theory
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Structures+in+M-Theory+2018"} Higher Structures in M-Theory 2018
                Fortschritte der Physik, Special Issue Volume 67, Issue 8-9 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02870"}> arXiv:1903.02870
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201910013"} doi:10.1002/prop.201910013
          %p
            Discussion of the CSFT-action as of the form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            is in section 4.4 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p
            From all this one might expect analogously a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            underlying closed superstring field theory. This does not seem to materialzed yet in the literature, though. The closest is maybe the structure described in
          %ul
            %li
              Yuji Okawa,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
              %em Heterotic string field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406212"}> arXiv:hep-th/0406212
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory and physics
            %li
              %p
                Enrico Perron Cabus:
                %em Co-algebraic methods for String Field Theory and Quantum Field Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.02753"}> arXiv:2511.02753
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#ReferencesOnYMTheoryAspects For Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            The idea that open strings on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            exhibit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            to
            = succeed "-gauge" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(N)
          %ul
            %li#Witten95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , section 3 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Bound States Of Strings And
                  = succeed "-Branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510135"} arXiv:hep-th/9510135
          %p There, this is called an “obvious guess” (first line on p. 8). Subsequently, most authors cite this obvious guess as a fact; for instance the review
          %ul
            %li#Myers03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Myers"}> Robert Myers
              , section 3 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Nonabelian Phenomena on D-branes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0303072"} arXiv:hep-th/0303072
          %p
            By actual computation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string+field+theory"} open string field theory
            “convincing evidence” (see bottom of p. 22) was found, numerically, in
          %ul
            %li#ColettiSigalovTaylor03
              Erasmo Coletti, Ilya Sigalov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Washington+Taylor"} Washington Taylor
              = succeed "," do
                %em Abelian and nonabelian vector field effective actions from string field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0306041"} arXiv:hep-th/0306041
          %p Similar numerical derivation, as well as exact derivation at zero momentum, is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"} Martin Schnabl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Yang-Mills Action from Open Superstring Field Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0307019"} arXiv:hep-th/0307019
          %p The first full derivation seems to be due to
          %ul
            %li#Lee16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
              ,
              %em Covariant open bosonic string field theory on multiple D-branes in the proper-time gauge
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.01473"}> arXiv:1609.01473
              )
          %p which is surveyed in
          %ul
            %li#Lee17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformation of the Cubic Open String Field Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06154"} arXiv:1701.06154
          %p
            That on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
            this reproduces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%28-1%29-branes"} D(-1)-branes
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/IKKT+matrix+model"} IKKT matrix model
            is shown in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
              ,
              %em
                Covariant Open String Field Theory on Multiple D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-Branes
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.06402"}> arXiv:1703.06402
              )
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"} L-infinity algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory"} higher Chern-Simons theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            that appears to lowest order as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+QFT"} effective QFT
            in open string field theory is for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Zeitlin"}> Anton Zeitlin
                ,
              %p
                %em Homotopy Lie Superalgebra in Yang-Mills Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.1773"}> arXiv:0708.1773
                )
              %p
                %em BV Yang-Mills as a Homotopy Chern-Simons via SFT
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.1411"}> arXiv:0709.1411
                )
              %p
                %em SFT-inspired Algebraic Structures in Gauge Theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.3843"}> arXiv:0711.3843
                )
              %p
                %em Conformal Field Theory and Algebraic Structure of Gauge Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.1840"}> arXiv:0812.1840
                )
          %h3#ReferencesBackgroundIndependence Background independence
          %p
            References discussing independence of string field theories on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            background) in terms of which they are written down.
          %h4#ReferencesBackgroundIndependenceForClosed For closed string field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                %em Quantum Background Independence of Closed String Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9311009"}> arXiv:hep-th/9311009
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                %em Background Independent Algebraic Structures in Closed String Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9408053"}> arXiv:hep-th/9408053
                )
          %p A review of the history of some related developments is given in
          %ul
            %li
              Sabbir Rahman,
              %em Manifest background independent formulation of string field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.natscience.com/Uwe/Forum.aspx/physics-research/503/Manifest-background-independent-formulation-of-string-field"}> newsgroup comment
              )
          %p
            Closed string field theory has also been argued to arise from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loops"} Wilson loops
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/IKKT+matrix+model"} IKKT matrix model
            in (
            %a{:href => "#FukumaKawaiKitazawaTsuchiya97"}> Fukuma-Kawai-Kitazawa-Tsuchiya 97
            )
          %ul
            %li#FukumaKawaiKitazawaTsuchiya97
              M. Fukuma, H. Kawai, Y. Kitazawa, A. Tsuchiya,
              = succeed "," do
                %em String Field Theory from IIB Matrix Model
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705128"} arXiv:hep-th/9705128
          %h4#for_open_string_field_theory For open string field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On background independent open string field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9208027"} arXiv:hep-th/9208027
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                , Carlo Maccaferri,
                %em String Field Theory Solution for Any Open String Background
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.3021"}> arXiv:1406.3021
                )
          %h3#BosonicStringVacuumAndSenConjecture Tachyon dynamics, decaying D-branes and Sen’s conjecture
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} Sen's conjecture
            about the open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon"} tachyon
            and the decay of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D25-brane"} D25-brane
            originates in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universality of the Tachyon Potential
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911116"} arXiv:hep-th/9911116
          %p
            Hints for the decay of the space-filling
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D25-brane"} D25-brane
            in open bosonic string field theory and the resulting closed string vacuum were discussed in articles like
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Ian Ellwood, Washington Taylor,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Open string field theory without open strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0103085"} arXiv:hep-th/0103085
            %li
              %p
                Bo Feng, Yang-Hui He, Nicolas Moeller,
                %em Testing the Uniqueness of the Open Bosonic String Field Theory Vacuum
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0103103"}> arXiv:hep-th/0103103
                )
          %p A breakthrough were then the analytic solutions describing the bosonic string tachyon vacuum in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"}> Martin Schnabl
                ,
                %em Analytic solution for tachyon condensation in open string field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0511286"}> arXiv:hep-th/0511286
                )
            %li
              %p
                Ian Ellwood,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"} Martin Schnabl
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proof of vanishing cohomology at the tachyon vacuum
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0606142"} arXiv:hep-th/0606142
          %p
            Analogous discussion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} Sen's conjecture
            including also brane/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-brane"} anti-brane
            pairs in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Rastelli"}> Leonardo Rastelli
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"} Ashoke Sen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                %em Vacuum String Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0106010"}> arXiv:hep-th/0106010
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tachyon Dynamics in Open String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0410103"} arXiv:hep-th/0410103
            %li
              %p
                L. Bonora, N. Bouatta, C. Maccaferri,
                %em Towards open-closed string duality: Closed Strings as Open String Fields
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0609182"}> arXiv:hep-th/0609182
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tachyon Vacuum in Cubic Superstring Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0707.4591"} arXiv:0707.4591
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Analytic Solution for Tachyon Condensation in Berkovits’ Open Superstring Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.4400"} arXiv:1308.4400
          %h3#relation_to_higher_spin_gauge_theory Relation to higher spin gauge theory
          %p
            The idea that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+spin+gauge+theory"} higher spin gauge theory
            appears as the limiting case of string field theory where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+tension"} string tension
            vanishes goes back to
          %ul
            %li#HenneauxTeitelboim87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
                = succeed "," do
                  %em First And Second Quantized Point Particles Of Any Spin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Zanelli"} Jorge Zanelli
                (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Santiago 1987, Proceedings, Quantum mechanics of fundamental systems 2
            %li#Gross88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gross"}> David Gross
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em High-Energy Symmetries Of String Theory
          %p and is further developed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#SagnottiTsulaia03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Augusto+Sagnotti"}> Augusto Sagnotti
                , M. Tsulaia,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On higher spins and the tensionless limit of String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0311257"} arXiv:hep-th/0311257
            %li#Bonelli03
              %p
                G. Bonelli,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Tensionless Limit of Bosonic Strings, Infinite Symmetries and Higher Spins
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0305155"} arXiv:hep-th/0305155
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Augusto+Sagnotti"}> Augusto Sagnotti
                , M. Taronna,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Lessons for Higher-Spin Interactions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.5242"} arXiv:1006.5242
            %li#Sagnotti11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Augusto+Sagnotti"}> Augusto Sagnotti
                ,
                %em Notes on Strings and Higher Spins
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1112.4285"}> arXiv:1112.4285
                )
          %p And conversely:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Rakibur Rahman, Massimo Taronna,
                %em From Higher Spins to Strings: A Primer
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Fredenhagen"} Stefan Fredenhagen
                (ed.)
                %em Introduction to Higher Spin Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.07932"}> arXiv:1512.07932
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Gaberdiel"}> Matthias Gaberdiel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rajesh+Gopakumar"} Rajesh Gopakumar
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Theory as a Higher Spin Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.07237"} arXiv:1512.07237
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP09(2016)085"} doi:10.1007/JHEP09(2016)085
        .revisedby
          %p
            Last revised on November  5, 2025 at 05:24:01.
